The Hon'ble Supreme Court of India, in Deepal Girishbhai Soni and ors., Vs. United India Insurance Company Limited 2 , while dealing with Section 163A of the Motor Vehicles Act, 1988 held as under:
Chapter XI was, thus, enacted for grant of immediate relief to a section of people whose annual income is not more than Rs. 40,000/- having regard to the fact that in terms of Section 163-A of the Act read with the Second Schedule appended thereto;
compensation is to be paid on a structured formula not only having regard to the age of the victim and his income but also the other factors relevant therefor.
